\tag{fdip}
\title{Pairings and discrete differences}
\date{2026-10-20}

\p{How can an edge difference return to a vertex field, and when does
its energy detect a constant field? The [finite field modules](fdip-0010)
and [counting duality](fdip-001F) give a concrete starting point.
Chosen perfect symmetric pairings extend the adjoint construction to
different modules over a commutative ring. Applied to incidence, they
give weighted energy and the cyclic kinetic factorization.}

\p{The [component-kernel theorem](fdip-0008) identifies the additional
role of positive real weights; a characteristic-two example shows why
perfection alone is insufficient. An [invertible precision](fdip-001Q)
then gives a unique response to each source, before any probability
interpretation.}

